# Claude Code copies a gitignored file that matches a pattern here into a new worktree.
# The format is the `.gitignore` format. See <https://code.claude.com/docs/en/worktrees.md>.

# `.gitignore` ignores the FoxIO corpus, because the corpus is FoxIO-licensed material.
# A new worktree therefore holds no corpus.
# Without the corpus, `make conformance` skips and `make cover` reads 0.6 points low.
# The measurement on 2026-08-13, at commit `83f2127` and at commit `7210e80`: `make cover`
# reports 75.0 percent with the corpus and 74.4 percent without it, at both commits.
# This comment read `coverage reads 2 points low` until then, and no measurement held it.
testdata/foxio/
